    "body": "Relay BB run pushed an update.\n\nPull request: #309\n\nTokens: 0 · Cost: $0.0000\n\nBranch `bb/relay-113-module-contract-07-12-enforce-module-a-thr_at7w2bgfe8` has been pushed to origin.\n\n## Summary\n\nCloses #113 — enforces module and service import boundaries via dependency-cruiser.\n\n- Added `backend/dependency-cruiser.rules.json` (shared rule set) and `backend/.dependency-cruiser.cjs` (config) defining `no-module-service-internal-cross-import`: a module or service under `modules/X/**` or `services/X/**` may only be imported by another module/service through its public entry point (`src/index.ts`); `packages/*` shared code stays unrestricted.\n- Exposed the check as `pnpm run check:boundaries` (backend), which scans the real `modules`/`services` directories and reports actionable diagnostics (importer, imported path, violated rule) with a non-zero exit code on violation.\n- Added a new `@semprec/module-boundaries` package wrapping the dependency-cruiser Node API, with fixture modules/services and a vitest suite proving: forbidden module↔module, service↔service, and cross-category internal imports are rejected, while public-entry, same-module-internal, and neutral shared-package imports pass — and that the violation report names importer, imported path, and rule.\n\n## Test plan\n\n- [x] `pnpm install --frozen-lockfile` (backend)\n- [x] `pnpm -r run build` (backend, all 8 workspace packages typecheck)\n- [x] `pnpm run test` (backend) — 25 test files, 320 tests passed\n- [x] `pnpm run check:boundaries` (backend) — 0 violations against real (currently empty) `modules`/`services`; manually verified it fails with correct diagnostics when a deliberate forbidden import is introduced\n- [x] Web workspace install/build/test unaffected (75 tests passed)\n\nRelay-Step-Status: pass",
