    "body": "Relay BB run pushed an update.\n\nPull request: #309\n\nTokens: 0 · Cost: $0.0000\n\nPushed to branch `bb/relay-113-module-contract-07-12-enforce-module-a-thr_at7w2bgfe8` (existing PR #309).\n\n## Summary\n\nCloses #113 — enforces module and service import boundaries via dependency-cruiser.\n\n- Added `backend/dependency-cruiser.rules.json` (shared rule set) and `backend/.dependency-cruiser.cjs` (config) defining `no-module-service-internal-cross-import`: a module or service under `modules/X/**` or `services/X/**` may only be imported by another module/service through its public entry point (`src/index.ts`); `packages/*` shared code stays unrestricted.\n- Exposed the check as `pnpm run check:boundaries` (backend), which scans the real `modules`/`services` directories and reports actionable diagnostics (importer, imported path, violated rule) with a non-zero exit code on violation.\n- Added a new `@semprec/module-boundaries` package wrapping the dependency-cruiser Node API, with fixture modules/services and a vitest suite proving all four forbidden internal cross-import directions (module↔module, service↔service, module→service, service→module) are rejected, and that public-entry/shared-package imports pass.\n- Addressed code review on PR #309: removed unused `formatViolations` dead API surface, typed the dependency-cruiser output with `ICruiseResult` instead of implicit `any`, and added the missing service→module internal-import fixture/test for full directional coverage.\n\n## Test plan\n\n- [x] `pnpm install --frozen-lockfile` (backend)\n- [x] `pnpm -r run build` (backend, all 8 workspace packages typecheck)\n- [x] `pnpm run test` (backend) — 34 test files, 429 tests passed\n- [x] `pnpm run check:boundaries` (backend) — 0 violations; manually verified it fails with correct diagnostics on a deliberate forbidden import\n- [x] Web workspace install/build/test — 9 test files, 81 tests passed\n\nRelay-Step-Status: pass",
